; Checkpoint Run -- an original maze-driving game.
; Load and play:  load "checkrun   checkrun
;
; See docs/checkpoint-run-design.md.  The encoded map is the only source of
; truth: collision, AI and the drawn road view all read it, and nothing reads
; canvas colour.  There are no picture assets.
;
; Three interpreter rules govern this file (design section 12):
;   * there is no >= or <=; write  not (a < b)
;   * a call's last argument absorbs trailing infix, so parenthesise:
;     (item :i :car.dir) * (item :i :car.offset)
;   * every drawing sequence lives inside one  ask 7 [...]

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Palette slots and shape slots.
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------

; Slot 255 is the reserved transparent index and cannot be a background, so
; off-road gets its own slot.  setup.palette defines every colour the game
; uses, which is why no asset needs to carry a palette.
make "cr.bg 244
make "cr.text 254
make "cr.turbo.c 253
make "cr.flag.c 252
make "cr.player.c 251
make "cr.road.c 250
make "cr.enemy.c 249
make "cr.smoke.c 248
make "cr.panel.c 247
make "cr.sand 246
make "cr.rock.c 245

make "sh.block 1
make "sh.player 2
make "sh.enemy 3
make "sh.flag 4
make "sh.turbo 5
make "sh.rock 6
make "sh.smoke 7
make "sh.crash 9
make "sh.mark 13

; Turtle y of the six instrument-band separators (design 2.1).
make "cr.bands [128 96 8 -32 -72 -112]

; Session high score: outlives a game, so it is set up once at load.
make "cr.high 0

; Last engine pitch played. Initialised here so a frame can run before
; setup.sound has been called (the tests drive play.frame directly).
make "cr.engine -1

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; World data.  Each world is a list of forty 32-character rows, appended one
; row per line.
;
; `load` only joins lines for a `to`...`end` procedure body -- every other
; line is executed on its own -- so a bracketed list literal cannot span
; lines in a loadable file.  Each row therefore gets a complete statement of
; its own.  LOAD_MAX_LINE is 256, and two globals beat eighty because
; MAX_GLOBAL_VARIABLES is 128 for the whole session.
;
; A row that were all digits would be read as a number and lose its leading
; zeros, so test_checkrun asserts every row is still 32 characters long.
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------

